  inbox arrives. One process, one SQLite file, no deploy story yet.

  src/
    server.ts          HTTP wiring only
    db/                connection, schema, migrations
    tasks/service.ts   the ONLY place task mutations happen
    tasks/routes.ts    HTTP surface
    events/types.ts    the semantic event catalogue (shared with the client)
    events/repo.ts     append + query
    users/             records, dev actor resolution
  web/                 index.html (grows from the existing file), app.ts

  The one load-bearing rule: [1mroutes never touch the database.[0m Every mutation goes through [38;5;153mtasks/service.ts[39m, which opens
  a transaction, writes the task change and its event together, and commits. That single chokepoint is what makes the
  event log trustworthy, and it's where subscription fan-out will later attach without disturbing anything above it.

  Since this is effectively a new project, tooling is cheapest to set up now, before there's code to retrofit:

